## CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia? | fragment 'compared with Nvidia' | kept in the fresh answer: True | statements written 4

I kept it under the evidence instruction to “Separately write a standalone summary in one_line” and the rule to keep “the company's own figure, guidance or decision”; the passage reports Nvidia’s revenue growth and margins. The closing check’s exclusion for “a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes” does not send this comparison back to the check: it excludes product or benchmark comparisons, not reported financial figures. As the senior analyst, these figures are relevant context for Nvidia’s competitive position and profitability, and I would file them under v1 for revenue growth, v3 for gross margin, and v10 for operating margin.
**The “one dial” conclusion is not supported. Some borderline cases remain difficult, but the design also contains separable defects: it confuses who speaks with what they say, lets neighboring claims supply a statement’s justification, and substitutes filing eligibility for evidence value.**

For example, Zuckerberg’s “slower-than-expected progress” is discarded because he represents a customer, while a journalist’s equally unquantified judgment avoids that check. That is a design error, not an unavoidable trade-off.

I read the complete stored v94 request, the governing sections, both gold files, the supplied probes, and raw answers beside their articles. No files changed and no paid calls ran. Proposed wording below is untested.

**1. The field design applies the wrong evidence rule to customer and competitor judgments. — Contradiction / design**

The design maps kind 3 to `analyst_or_outlet`, although the standard says **a named party’s claim or estimate**, not just an analyst’s. Its implementation rejects:

> `if e['party'] in RELATED_PARTIES and e.get('scale', 'none') == 'none'`

See [design-v78-fields.md:14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md:14) and [extraction.py:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:210).

**Stored example.** In [poc-v100-supporting-41.json](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/sends/poc-v100-supporting-41.json), article `gnews:c675…`, third answer, `e15`, Zuckerberg’s slower-than-expected agent progress is correctly recognized as `new/judgement`, but classified `customer/none`. The code therefore rejects it. The [gold keeps it as supporting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/golden-v5-dev.json:16023). Lisa Su’s customer forecasts exceeding expectations suffer the same problem.

The governing distinction is between **actions/operating figures** and **claims/estimates**, not between customer executives and professional analysts: [standard §5.1, lines 375–376](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:375).

**Alternative formulation:**

> “Identify what the statement asserts separately from the speaker’s relationship to the company. A customer or competitor can make a specific claim or estimate. Judge that claim under the named-party rule; do not reject it solely because it lacks an amount or date.”

**Predicted effect.** Recovers these named judgments without admitting partner lists. Simply removing the rejection would also admit noise: among nine raw records triggering this predicate across the two v100 files, Corning’s generic “world needs our glass optical fiber” also appears. Thus the correction must preserve the specific-claim test. No kept matter needs to be lost.

**2. The role’s procedure still contradicts the standard; changing exception precedence did not resolve it. — Contradiction**

The role says:

> “A material statement is one of four kinds.”

> “take it only when it has a kind and nothing on the list applies.”

The closing check says:

> “Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item.”

See [role-v74.txt:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74.txt:4) and [review-v74.txt:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/review-v74.txt:1).

The standard explicitly says the four kinds **describe** evidence; acceptance comes from the analyst’s judgment, including each rejection’s boundary: [§5.1, lines 370–372](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:370).

**Stored example.** The v94 Nations-blog answer, archive call `186`, keeps ThinkDeep, Sarvam and Widelabs as evidence. Each describes an existing service. The [gold rejects all three under D250’s arrangement rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/golden-v5-dev.json:6949). Their names and reported benefits satisfy the role’s recognizable shapes without establishing a new step.

The author’s v77 experiment made “has a kind” the default reason to retain a statement and removed the closing warning. Its increased noise therefore does not exhaust sentence-level remedies.

**Alternative formulation:**

> “For each research matter, identify the new event, figure or specific judgment an analyst would record. Apply §5.3’s exclusions with their own boundaries. An exception removes only that exclusion; it does not establish that the statement should be kept. Retain every matter that passes.”

**Predicted effect.** Reduces existing-arrangement noise while preserving genuine adoptions without amounts. The “eight statements” sentence is not itself wrong; its antecedent must mean eight statements passing this test. A blanket “reject partner lists” substitute would lose the kept EY/Abridge/Amdocs/Box matter.

**3. The decision attaches to an entire quote rather than the particular assertion it justifies. — Design / missing**

The role says:

> “One evidence item records one statement. Copy its quote verbatim…”

The closing check exempts adoption:

> “also when a comparison shares its sentence”

See [role-v74.txt:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74.txt:16) and [review-v74.txt:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/review-v74.txt:5).

**Stored examples.**

- V94 archive call `223`, `e1`, quotes “Nvidia remains the king” alongside revenue-growth figures. Its summary asserts the figures, not leadership.
- In v100’s Nemotron-blog third answer, the quote contains both LangChain’s integration and its benchmark comparison. The whole record becomes `product_comparison_or_detail` and is rejected, losing the kept integration.
- The [common-knowledge probe:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/probe-v80-common-knowledge.txt:3) explicitly justifies the “king” passage using the neighboring financial figures.

The standard already distinguishes the adoption from its accompanying comparison, and records **one matter**, not necessarily one grammatical sentence: [D250 items 3 and 5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:229).

**Alternative formulation:**

> “Decide which research matter this record preserves. Apply the evidence test to that assertion. Retain the quoted context needed to understand it, but do not let an adjacent number, date or comparison justify another assertion. A comparison accompanying a qualifying adoption does not erase the adoption.”

**Predicted effect.** Preserves integrations while reducing independently summarized characterizations. It need not lose any kept matter. A shortest-quote rule would risk losing conditions and attribution; I do not recommend one.

The reported **13 of 33** mixed-quote cases are consequently not proof of 13 independent bad decisions. D250’s existing counting rule already requires examining what each record preserves. No ruler change is needed.

**4. “Known” conflates a statement’s age, its disclosure date and its continuing relevance. — Contradiction / abstract**

The closing check asks:

> “whether it is new”

The v80 definition goes further:

> “reported as recent (days or weeks, not an earlier month or year)”

See [review-v74.txt:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/review-v74.txt:1) and [extraction.py:162](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:162).

**Stored examples.** The [v79 probes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/probe-v79-newness.txt:1) reject Beijing’s refusal as an existing position and the design cancellation because another report appeared the previous week. V80 rejects Omniverse’s licensing change as `known`, although the article distinguishes the May effective date from the July announcement.

The standard supplies an operational rule despite unavailable company memory: judge retelling from **text and dates**, do not presume it when unclear, and preserve still-effective guidance, forecasts and plans: [§5.3:400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:400).

**Alternative formulation:**

> “Distinguish when the underlying event occurred from when this item reports it. Do not infer that a statement was already known merely because the project began earlier or the item cites another report. Apply the separate rules for an existing arrangement, a retold actual figure, and guidance or plans still in force.”

**Predicted effect.** Recovers recent disclosures and continuing guidance without reopening clearly retrospective arrangements. A compulsory recent-date test would lose the kept DeepSeek project, underway for a year, and LG’s discussions “last month.” The wording cannot perfectly resolve every undated arrangement.

**5. Filing is being used as the evidence test, and “relationship” is being substituted for a causal path. — Abstract / design**

The role calls each `takes` line:

> “the one rule for what belongs in that question’s file”

The schema permits an empty link:

> “however important it sounds.”

See [role-v74.txt:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74.txt:1) and [placement.py:60–64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/placement.py:60).

**Stored example.** The [debt-raising probe:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/probe-v75-residue.txt:18) first recognizes NVIDIA’s financing plan as evidence, then says it should be omitted because it does not concern demand, supply, competition or pricing. That is the filing vocabulary replacing the evidence rule.

Conversely, the author’s proposed “the path is the relation itself” is too broad. D250 requires a path from **this matter** to a question; being a supplier does not make everything the supplier does relevant. [Standard §5.3:405](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:405).

**Alternative formulation:**

> “First establish why this statement is evidence under §5.1–5.3. Then file it under the narrowest covered question, considering that question’s actual quantity or event. Explain the connection through what the statement changes; a shared company, industry or ecosystem is insufficient. An unfiled statement is dropped under D209, not reclassified as background.”

# Current state

As of October 30, 2026, the close-out of the extraction-quality phase; decisions through D246. Governing design: `docs/system-design.html` and `docs/prd/`; the extraction step's standard is [`prd/05-extraction-standard.html`](prd/05-extraction-standard.html) (D243). Every status paragraph of the phase, with its numbers, is in [the snapshot before this close-out](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/current-state.before-closeout-2026-10-30.md); earlier snapshots are linked there. They are records, not work orders.

## What runs, and which code is the latest

- **Latest pipeline code:** this branch, `fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28`, stacked on `feat/thesis-admission-v12` and `feat/parallel-day`; all three pushed, none merged into `main`. `main` has the newer service, UI and Idea code (3 commits this branch lacks) and still replays `poc-v23` (extraction v10).
- **Default configuration:** `poc/config/poc-v94.json` (D267, 2026-11-02, Alex's words there, making it the default; it is poc-v92, the version he fixed under D265, with the three D266 fixes: review-v74, the narrowest rule, the widened quote repair): extraction v74 on `gpt-6-luna`, the one decider (D264): the request shows the questions open at the start of the item's day with their code-written takes lines (`placement.question_lines`), the schema defines `links` by the filing rule (`placement.FILING_RULE`), the extraction files each statement by its links and no placement call is made; a statement linked to nothing is dropped as `no home` (D209); a statement under a driver and its root keeps the driver (`extraction.narrowest_links`, D207 in code); the role text is role-v66's with one paragraph on the open questions, the request ends with v66's check; Jev matching with the collision judge `collision-v2` (D190, D258); judging-v7 with the theme block and the evidence in view (D195, D198, D263). `scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test and the README name it. Every later change is a new extraction number (v75 …) and a new `poc` configuration built from v94, measured against v94's three draws of 2026-11-02 (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/r7-combined-v94/`); `poc-v92` and its draws remain the record of the architecture's first measurement. `poc-v69` (role-v53 with the placement call) is the record of the previous architecture.
**One next task (2026-11-03, D271):** extraction v74d (`poc-v103`) carries the deep-review fixes on the v94 text and is the candidate: on 50 stored articles, three sends each against v94's three draws, gold matters reaching 132 → 146 and noise 95 → 89 (71 → 56 with long quotes that also carry a kept matter set apart; `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md` §12). Whether it replaces `poc-v94` as the default is Alex's word; no whole-bench run unless he asks. Residual noise: arrangements in place the text does not mark as old, journalist framing, a rival's long-standing share figure.
- **Moving the run to another machine (2026-11-01):** what is in Git, what is not (the corpus database, the end-to-end run folders, the answer stores), the sizes, the backup archive with its hash, and the portable launcher `research/2026-10-31-reference-context/run_seedv2.sh` for the three seed-v2 draws are in [`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/handoff-move-2026-11-01.md`](research/2026-10-31-reference-context/handoff-move-2026-11-01.md).
- Tests: full suite 241 passed; `docs/check.py` passes. The close-out code review (a blind reviewer, 13 findings) is answered below.

## The phase, 2026-10-28 to 2026-10-30

The three-month run was stopped on evidence bloat (D206). The extraction step was then rebuilt and measured alone, through its own harness:

1. Placement and drops (D207–D209): a separate placement call files statements; a statement no question takes is dropped with its reason and evaluation reads the drops.
2. The request no longer depends on the ledger (D211): the read is prepared early and filed at the item's turn.
3. One ruler (D229, D241, D243): the extraction standard signed by Alex, a golden set of 118 development articles and a frozen test set of 30, the scorer reading only the frozen gold (D244).
4. The prompt is a general hedge-fund brain (D237) and was iterated class by class on the direct read (D238): role-v29 (D239), role-v42 (D245, gold-rejected statements kept −26% at equal core), role-v51 (D246, must-not questions on small products 20 → 0 over 15 draws).
5. A quality read beyond the ruler (2026-10-30, [results](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/quality-2026-10-30/results.md)): four independent model readers read 24 random articles as analysts. The logs are [the loop log](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/loop-log.md) (rows 1–23) and [the direct-read log](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/loop-2026-10-29/log.md).

Where role-v51 stands (development set, three draws): core kept 77–81 of 86 per draw and the same in every draw (89% of core statements); supporting at least two draws 154 of 181; statements per draw 534 (role-v23: 833); numbers in the summary lines faithful (no invented figure in 2,065); about $0.0011 and 12.5 s per article.

## Open defects, to fix next

Each has its census; the extraction ones are classes for the loop of AGENTS §7.3 (one class at a time, the whole bench, read every regression).

Extraction (step 1), role-v51:

1. **Record fields when an article retells an earlier announcement**: role-v53 adopted (D247) ([loop log](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/loop-log.md) rows 26–30, [folder](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/fields-2026-10-30/)). Mechanism (five probes): the prompt's one clause "for a retelling, the original speaker and statement day" was read as "a statement the item explicitly attributes", so an action the item narrates got the outlet as speaker and the report day as its day, while the true day went to `event_time`, which no step reads. role-v52 (`poc-v68`) wrote the three fields' definitions into the role text: fields fixed, but about 7 to 15 more gold-rejected statements kept per draw (two runs). role-v53 (`poc-v69`) keeps role-v51's text and carries the same definitions as schema field descriptions (`extraction.FIELD_NOTES`, from version 53): in the simultaneous run U, outlet-as-speaker and report-day signals over 148 articles × 3 draws 166 → 35, verified field errors on a fresh blind read of 24 articles 18/96 → 11/94 records, gold-rejected kept −6.7 per draw, core and supporting within noise (the two largest core "losses" are the same matter quoted by another sentence). Left over: a column restating two companies' reported figures still credited to its author; unnamed executives tiered as third-party views (the tier table says rumour); days weaker than role-v52 (13 against 3 signals).
2. **Summary lines** lose a condition or say more than the quote in 11 of 102 (the Groq "acquisition" in quotation marks written as an acquisition; a deal's "backstop" link left in a neighbouring record); one event is split into several records in 9 (one Reuters rumour as three records).
3. **Noise, then placement recall.** Measured end to end 2026-10-31 (`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/e2e_compare.py`, three draws, 118 gold articles): the extraction's gold-rejected statements are mostly removed by the placement step, so about 20 noise pieces an estimate, of some 137 reaching judgement, remain per draw; the extraction-layer noise arms (role-v54…v70) are closed, default role-v53. The live defect is the placement step's recall: it drops a third of the core matters (26 of 86 a draw with ten seeds, 21 with `placement-narrow-v2`) because no open question takes them, and the ten hand-written seeds cover a third of the drivers; the fix is D208's seeded layer, generated from the watch list, with Alex's three calls in One next task. The extraction-layer record, for reference: measured on a fixed ruler. The ruler (D250): standard version 5 (four evidence boundaries and the counting unit, Alex's leans), gold `golden-v5/` re-derived by two blind readers with 62 recorded changes, and `final_scores.py` now refuses a gold whose evidence part was made for another version (it had scored every round since D248 on the version-3 gold). On that ruler, development set, three draws, versions sent together, blind-corrected: role-v63 against role-v53 (run Y3) gold-rejected kept per draw 108.7 → 83.0, core every draw 70 → 72, supporting at least two draws 128 → 128 (counting aid); role-v64 against v63 (Y4) 86.7 → 73.7, core 73 → 71, supporting 126 → 122; role-v65 against v64 (Y5) 73.0 → 59.3, core 71 → 71, supporting 120 → 123. Mechanism left: in the one-call check, an exception written on one row is read as a keep rule over the others (v63's closing list; v65's adoption exception over D250 item 1), so the 45 entries D250 moved out of the kept column are still kept 27 times per draw; a draft (not audited, not sent, `research/2026-10-30-noise/drafts/review-v66-draft.txt`; the number 66 later went to R3's role-v66, a different text, see One next task) scopes the adoption exception to a new step. Sealed on 2026-10-31 at the tag `extraction-noise-sealed-2026-10-31`; what can be resumed and reused (ruler, gold and its sha256, prompt versions, local answer stores with their sha256, tools and their use, open work, recovery commands) is in `research/2026-10-30-noise/SEALED-2026-10-31.md`. Loop log rows 34–53, `research/2026-10-30-noise/ruler-check-2026-10-31.md`.
4. **Questions**, read from the candidates themselves: DRAM contract prices (development) and the $12.9B Hugging Face acquisition (test) are opened in no draw, though the Hugging Face statement is kept in every draw; the OpenAI Ohio lease guarantee is never its own yes/no question, only covered by the wider lease-guarantee amount question; data-centre revenue for FY2028 is asked as total revenue growth (2 of 3 draws); per page the opening varies (the credit-support question on one page in 2 of 3 draws, carried by other pages in every draw). Must-not: the lidar-legislation policy question in 1 of 3 draws (role-v42: 11 of 15); one Nigeria production question in one draw.
5. **Whole statements lost:** 28 quotes refused by the quote check in three draws, every one read: 14 stitch parts of different sentences (the Palantir–Nemotron statement, the China H200 permission), 9 change a word or two at an edge ("the company" written as "Nvidia", "As a result" as "So"; among them the core "Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment" and "Vera CPU expected to bring $20 billion"), 2 are titles not in the body, 1 skips words with an ellipsis, 1 writes "85 percent" as "85%", 1 is a real misquote rightly refused. One whole-page empty answer on a page with 3 core entries (Micron, draw 1).
6. **The test set is small:** 9 core entries and 3 must-open questions; it shows no overfitting and little more.

Readers' doubts about the standard itself (for Alex; nothing changed): unsized named actions keep every small press release (D240); the optional Singapore case lets eleven asset records through (D231); the tier table has no row for an official's allegation, a company forecasting its own industry, or a research firm reporting a non-public action; a repeated old figure is kept at full weight each time (D243 #6) while a repeat is not new evidence (AGENTS §8). A fourth doubt, that "unknown" loses the "said by the report day" bound, is answered: every record keeps its item's publication day.

